465:# Part 3: Verifying a rule once (B2)
467:## 13. What a rule claims
473:- i32 operators: `binop(op, a, b)` (`evaluate.ts:266`), which throws `Trap` on division by zero and on −2³¹ / −1; shift counts are masked to five bits (`MASK = 31`, `evaluate.ts:265`).
476:For reduced-width checking, the verifier needs the integer operators at width `w` (Proposed: `binopW(op, a, b, w)` in `src/typed/rules/semantics.ts`): values are `w`-bit two's complement integers, results wrap to `w` bits, shift counts are masked to `log2 w` bits, the trap conditions use −2^(w−1). At `w = 32` `binopW` must equal `binop` exactly; a test checks it on boundary values and random pairs.
