297:## 10. What the mutation measurements say (IRWB-005)
299:IRWB-005 measured the gate by **mutation testing**: it manufactured wrong programs by changing one site of an accepted revision (a constant by one, a comparison flipped or weakened, operands swapped, a shift amount changed, a bounds check dropped or weakened, a trapping statement hoisted, an f32 operator or constant changed, a store dropped; `src/typed/mutate.ts` (IRWB-005)), judged each mutant with the gate exactly as a pass is judged, and classified every mutant a gate accepted as wrong or equivalent with a cascade of exhaustive, large-sample and unconstrained searches. The **kill rate** is killed / (killed + accepted wrong); its upper bound excludes mutants presumed equivalent.
